The Audi Q2 Technik trim was an entry-level option that replaced the SE trim in some markets, though it has been dropped for 2025 models in some regions. It typically came with the 1.0L 30 TFSI engine. I will evaluate based on the 30 TFSI engine with features standard on the Technik trim from around 2020-2024, incorporating the latest standard features where applicable, such as the 2024 updates.

**Cost & Risk:**
*   `price_usd`: The Technik trim was positioned above the base SE but below Sport/S line. A 2022 Technik 30 TFSI was listed around £20,049 used. New Q2 prices start around £29,765 (~$38,000 USD). Compared to the $52,000 market average for a *new* car, the Technik's price when new was below average. Score: 0.10.
